{
  "inShort": "The checkpoint ends behind: the playable-slice goal was missed. The devlog links show scenery and an art-reference thumbnail, not a playable build or five-player test notes. Mia stopped confirming work after week one, leaving co-op engineering capacity unconfirmed.",
  "discussed": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmvtkk82008ybnxz84yy1bm59",
      "text": "A public repository of the Godot demo projects the game builds on is done. The checked repository supplies demo folders, an MIT license and import instructions. It does not establish this game’s playable slice."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvtkk85q08ycnxz8fmvua13e",
      "text": "An animated reference video for the art style remains done. The sprint reused its link, whose title and thumbnail identify Big Buck Bunny. The video was not watched, so its suitability remains unverified. It does not demonstrate game footage."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvtkk88z08ydnxz8c8d2wj8p",
      "text": "A reference article on what playtesting is, for the team to read is done. The checked article explains playtesting and its formats. It supplies guidance, not evidence of the reported five-player test."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvtkk8ba08yenxz88uslzctv",
      "text": "A private design board for the team remains done. Its contents were not checked, so they establish nothing further about the playable slice."
    }
  ],
  "notDiscussed": [],
  "outsidePlan": [
    "The mountain photograph does not show the game’s tides or islands. No new artifact supports the reported polish or completed game video.",
    "No accessible build or test notes establish two playable islands, the tide loop, co-op sailing or what five players learned."
  ],
  "questions": [
    "Which build and test records support the reported playable features and five-player testing?"
  ]
}

